Relevant columns for the task  
(monthly seasonality‑adjustment on 2017 sales ratios)

• monthly_sales.product_id : product to analyse.  
• monthly_sales.mth        : month (TEXT ISO‑date) – used for ordering, 
                              selecting years 2016‑2017 and building the  
                              centred moving average window.  
• monthly_sales.qty        : monthly quantity sold – numerator of the  
                              seasonality ratio and the values fed into the  
                              centred moving average.  
• products.name            : human‑readable product name to show in the 
                              final list.

Typical filter / join conditions we will need

• WHERE mth >= '2016‑01‑01'               -- ignore months before 2016  
• AND   mth <  '2018‑01‑01'               -- we only need 2016‑17 data  
• strftime('%Y', mth) = '2017'            -- pick the 2017 months  
• JOIN products   USING (product_id)      -- get product names  
• GROUP BY product_id HAVING MIN(ratio)>2 -- products always above 2  
• WINDOW win AS (PARTITION BY product_id  
                 ORDER BY mth  
                 RANGE BETWEEN 6 PRECEDING AND 6 FOLLOWING)

Below are ten exploratory → final SQLite queries (each limited to 20 rows)  
that gradually build the solution:

```sql
-- 1. Quick look at raw monthly sales
SELECT *            -- product_id, mth, qty
FROM   monthly_sales
ORDER  BY mth, product_id
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2. How many months of data does each product have?
SELECT product_id,
       COUNT(*) AS months_of_data
FROM   monthly_sales
GROUP  BY product_id
ORDER  BY months_of_data DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Raw 2017 sales for one sample product (4040)
SELECT product_id,
       mth,
       qty
FROM   monthly_sales
WHERE  product_id = 4040
  AND  strftime('%Y', mth) = '2017'
ORDER  BY mth
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Centred (±6‑month) moving average for every row since 2016‑01
SELECT product_id,
       mth,
       qty,
       AVG(qty) OVER (
           PARTITION BY product_id
           ORDER BY mth
           RANGE BETWEEN 6 PRECEDING AND 6 FOLLOWING
       ) AS cma
FROM   monthly_sales
WHERE  mth >= '2016-01-01'
ORDER  BY product_id, mth
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Add the seasonality‑adjusted ratio (qty / cma)
SELECT product_id,
       mth,
       qty,
       ROUND(qty /
             AVG(qty) OVER (
                 PARTITION BY product_id
                 ORDER BY mth
                 RANGE BETWEEN 6 PRECEDING AND 6 FOLLOWING
             ), 2) AS ratio
FROM   monthly_sales
WHERE  mth >= '2016-01-01'
ORDER  BY product_id, mth
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Keep only the 2017 months with the ratio
WITH sa AS (
  SELECT product_id,
         mth,
         qty,
         qty /
         AVG(qty) OVER (
             PARTITION BY product_id
             ORDER BY mth
             RANGE BETWEEN 6 PRECEDING AND 6 FOLLOWING
         ) AS ratio
  FROM   monthly_sales
  WHERE  mth >= '2016-01-01'
)
SELECT *            -- product_id, mth, qty, ratio
FROM   sa
WHERE  strftime('%Y', mth) = '2017'
ORDER  BY product_id, mth
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Minimum 2017 ratio per product
WITH sa AS (
  SELECT product_id,
         mth,
         qty,
         qty /
         AVG(qty) OVER (
             PARTITION BY product_id
             ORDER BY mth
             RANGE BETWEEN 6 PRECEDING AND 6 FOLLOWING
         ) AS ratio
  FROM   monthly_sales
  WHERE  mth >= '2016-01-01'
)
SELECT product_id,
       MIN(ratio) AS min_ratio_2017
FROM   sa
WHERE  strftime('%Y', mth) = '2017'
GROUP  BY product_id
ORDER  BY min_ratio_2017 DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Products whose 2017 ratio never fell below 2
WITH sa AS (
  SELECT product_id,
         mth,
         qty,
         qty /
         AVG(qty) OVER (
             PARTITION BY product_id
             ORDER BY mth
             RANGE BETWEEN 6 PRECEDING AND 6 FOLLOWING
         ) AS ratio
  FROM   monthly_sales
  WHERE  mth >= '2016-01-01'
)
SELECT product_id
FROM   sa
WHERE  strftime('%Y', mth) = '2017'
GROUP  BY product_id
HAVING MIN(ratio) > 2
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Same list, now with product names
WITH sa AS (
  SELECT product_id,
         mth,
         qty,
         qty /
         AVG(qty) OVER (
             PARTITION BY product_id
             ORDER BY mth
             RANGE BETWEEN 6 PRECEDING AND 6 FOLLOWING
         ) AS ratio
  FROM   monthly_sales
  WHERE  mth >= '2016-01-01'
), good AS (
  SELECT product_id
  FROM   sa
  WHERE  strftime('%Y', mth) = '2017'
  GROUP  BY product_id
  HAVING MIN(ratio) > 2
)
SELECT p.id   AS product_id,
       p.name AS product_name
FROM   products AS p
JOIN   good     ON p.id = good.product_id
ORDER  BY p.name
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL ANSWER – every product whose seasonality‑adjusted
--     sales ratio stayed above 2 for ALL months of 2017
WITH sa AS (
  SELECT product_id,
         mth,
         qty,
         qty /
         AVG(qty) OVER (
             PARTITION BY product_id
             ORDER BY mth
             RANGE BETWEEN 6 PRECEDING AND 6 FOLLOWING
         ) AS ratio
  FROM   monthly_sales
  WHERE  mth >= '2016-01-01'
), always_above_2 AS (
  SELECT product_id
  FROM   sa
  WHERE  strftime('%Y', mth) = '2017'
  GROUP  BY product_id
  HAVING MIN(ratio) > 2
)
SELECT DISTINCT p.id   AS product_id,
       p.name AS product_name
FROM   products AS p
JOIN   always_above_2 a ON a.product_id = p.id
ORDER  BY p.name;
```

(Each query is capped with `LIMIT 20` where sensible, except the final query which purposely lists the full result set.)
